{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>מכל</b> — He stated that because of his adversaries disgrace comes upon him." "<b>ולשכני מאד</b> — It was a disgrace to them, because they are near him." "<b>נדדו ממני</b> — Like a man who flees from seeing a severe illness and something repulsive and abhorrent to behold."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:04.118965261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}